Subject: [candle] nax-tensor-op-kernels

  MLX's NAX fragment and tile helpers (mlx b6368984, nax.metal, prepended to the sdpa and quantized sources) and its NAX attention kernels beside the steel one, dispatched as MLX does — head dims 128 and 256 on a bf16 query, the head-dim split kernel at 256; the tensor-op GEMM over the fork's dequantisers rides the quantized subject
  Also the steel kernel's causal K/V loop bound, clamped to the key tile count: unclamped, a tile-unaligned query length ran the loop past kL and read beyond the K/V buffers, invisible until the bytes past a buffer were NaN.

Applies to: 0.10.2
Files: 4

